CS 214 Project III: A Simple Shell

Partners
--------
aa3281
ac2945

Design notes
------------
The program reads commands with read() and uses the same loop for interactive
and batch modes. It splits each command into tokens and stores the arguments
in resizable lists. The shell uses fork(), execv(), waitpid(), pipe(), and
dup2() to run commands and pipelines.

The built-in commands are cd, pwd, which, and exit. Other commands are
searched for in /usr/local/bin, /usr/bin, and /bin. The program supports input
and output redirection. In batch mode, child processes use /dev/null for
standard input.

Wildcard tokens are expanded by looking through the correct directory.
Comments, empty commands, syntax errors, and wildcards with no matches are
also handled.

Testing strategy
----------------
The test script checks external commands, the built-in commands, input and
output redirection, pipelines, and wildcard expansion. It also checks comments,
empty commands, syntax errors, missing commands, batch-mode input from a file,
and the /dev/null standard input used by child processes.